{
  "requirements": [
    {
      "statement": "The withdrawal of consent does not affect any sharing of health information that was carried out under consent prior to the withdrawal.",
      "citations": [
        "dha-consent-access-standard-2025#0018"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Any entity that accessed or received health information via the Health Information System (HIS) prior to the revocation of consent and incorporated that information into its records may retain that information.",
      "citations": [
        "dha-consent-access-standard-2025#0018"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If a patient opts out of the Health Information System (HIS), personal health information should continue to be received by the HIS from the entity, but patient identifiers must be anonymized in accordance with UAE Federal Law No. (45) of 2021 and the Policy for Health Data Protection and Confidentiality.",
      "citations": [
        "dha-consent-access-standard-2025#0018"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Following an opt-out from the Health Information System (HIS), personal health information should not be retrieved using 'Break the Glass' (BTG) access.",
      "citations": [
        "dha-consent-access-standard-2025#0018"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [],
  "gaps": [],
  "comparisons": [
    {
      "statement": "Under EU GDPR, the withdrawal of consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal.",
      "citations": [
        "eu-gdpr-2016-679#0092",
        "eu-gdpr-2016-679#0102"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "The provided rules are specific to the Dubai Health Authority (DHA) Standards for Health Information Consent and Access Control (2025) and UAE Federal Law No. (45) of 2021. These rules apply to the Dubai health information exchange (NABIDH).",
    "The status of information already shared is explicitly addressed by the DHA standards, which permit the retention of information already incorporated into records prior to revocation."
  ]
}
```

